  "description": "The option keys a catalogue version 2 variant names its options by (docs/protocol/network.md §4.18, catalogue version 2): each key's meaning, its label in five languages, the Google Merchant Center attribute it fills on an export (gmc), and other spellings a reader takes as the key (also). An option is {key, name, value}: the key is one of these, or any other lower-case name (^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,39}$), which is the business's own; the name is the business's own label, in its own language; the value is as the business writes it. A producer may write a key or any of its also spellings; a reader takes an also spelling as the key (colour is color) before anything else, then compares keys and values exactly. A key is never removed or renamed, and a spelling never moves to another key.",
